spec:
  grid: 10x10 or 15x15 [observed]; background 0
  grey_blocks:
    shape: solid 2x2 grey (color 5) anchors
    count: 3-6
    separation: min Chebyshev distance >=3 between any two block cells
    placement: most interior; 0-1 blocks may touch grid edge (partial frame OK)
  singletons:
    type: single colored pixels (not grey, not bg)
    count: 5-12; ratio to blocks ~0.8-3.0
    colors: 4-7 distinct non-grey non-bg colors; duplicates allowed (up to 4 of one color)
    placement: scattered on bg cells, not on grey or frame cells (except rare already-in-frame OK)
    min_dist_to_nearest_frame: 0-4 Chebyshev; typically 1-2
    isolation: may be 8-adjacent to other singletons (not required to be isolated)
  output_rule: |
    Each singleton moves to a cell in the 1-cell Chebyshev frame of a grey block.
    Destination = clamp(singleton_pos, block_frame), i.e. row/col clamped to [r0-1,r1+1]x[c0-1,c1+1].
    For diagonally-outside singletons with an exact 8-dir sightline hitting grey, the
    cell just before the first grey pixel on that ray is an alternative destination.
    Assignment minimizes total king-move distance (Hungarian); each frame cell used at most once.
    Grey blocks and bg preserved; singleton source cells cleared.

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size (10x10 or 15x15) and place 3-6 grey 2x2 blocks with min pairwise Chebyshev >=3.
    2. For each block, decide 0-5 frame cells to fill (total filled = desired singleton count, 5-12).
       Assign a random non-grey non-bg color to each filled frame cell. This is the output.
    3. For each filled frame cell, compute the inverse displacement to derive the input singleton position.
       Move the singleton away from the block along the clamp axis (outward), placing it 1-4 cells away
       on a free bg cell. For corner frame cells, optionally use diagonal sightline (reverse the ray).
    4. Verify no singleton lands on another singleton, grey cell, or out of bounds. Retry placement if needed.
    5. Clear the frame cells to get the input grid (grey blocks + scattered singletons on bg).
```
